{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":24,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.segmentBoundary_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.segmentBoundary_swap","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L222-L225","doc":"**Reverse orientation** flips the boundary to its inverse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.segmentBoundary_glue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.segmentBoundary_glue","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L213-L220","doc":"**Gluing law (subdivision additivity of Stokes).**  Two adjacent\nsegments sharing the middle rung `b` compose: the boundary of `a..c` is\nthe ordered product of the boundaries `b..c` and `a..b` (the shared\ninternal transport `g b` cancels).  Iterating this glues a whole tiling\nfrom its plaquettes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.stripHolonomy_eq_segmentBoundary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.stripHolonomy_eq_segmentBoundary","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L208-L211","doc":"The strip holonomy is the boundary of the segment `0..n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.segmentBoundary_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.segmentBoundary_self","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L204-L206","doc":"A degenerate segment (`a = a`) has trivial boundary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.segmentBoundary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.segmentBoundary","kind":"def","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L200-L202","doc":"Boundary holonomy of the strip segment spanning rungs `a..b`,\n`g b · g a⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.isFlatPlaquette_strip_flat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.isFlatPlaquette_strip_flat","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L185-L188","doc":"The boundary of a flat strip is a flat plaquette. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.stripHolonomy_flat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.stripHolonomy_flat","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L177-L183","doc":"A **flat** strip — constant parallel transport `g ≡ g 0`, i.e. every\nbased curvature is trivial — has trivial boundary holonomy.  Recovers\n`loopHolonomyPureGauge_eq_one` (the closed loop) as the flat closed\nstrip. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.stripHolonomy_telescope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.stripHolonomy_telescope","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L166-L175","doc":"**Discrete non-abelian Stokes for a strip.**  The ordered product of\nthe based plaquette curvatures telescopes to the boundary holonomy\n`g_n · g_0⁻¹`: the internal transports `gᵢ` (`0 < i < n`) cancel\npairwise, leaving only the outer boundary.  A non-abelian discrete\nfundamental theorem of calculus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.stripHolonomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.stripHolonomy","kind":"def","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L159-L164","doc":"**Strip holonomy**: the ordered product of the based plaquette\ncurvatures `F_{n-1} · … · F₁ · F₀` over a strip of `n` plaquettes\n(later plaquettes on the left, path order). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.basedCurvature","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.basedCurvature","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L155-L157","doc":"**Based curvature of plaquette `i`** in a strip: the increment of the\nparallel transport `g` between consecutive rungs, `Fᵢ = g_{i+1} · gᵢ⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.holonomy_perm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.holonomy_perm","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L135-L142","doc":"**Abelian degeneration** (`CommMonoid`): the path-ordering of the\nholonomy collapses — reordering the segments (deforming the path in the\ncommutative limit) leaves the holonomy unchanged.  This is the classical\nlimit where Yekutieli's non-abelian Stokes reduces to ordinary\n(abelian) Stokes and the surface-ordering is irrelevant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.isFlatPlaquette_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.isFlatPlaquette_conj","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L126-L133","doc":"**Gauge invariance of flatness.**  A gauge transformation acts on a\nbased-loop holonomy by conjugation `b ↦ u * b * u⁻¹`; the curvature\ndefect is gauge-*covariant*, so its vanishing (flatness) is\ngauge-*invariant*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.isFlatPlaquette_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.isFlatPlaquette_mul","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L117-L124","doc":"**Flatness is closed under composition.**  Concatenating two flat loops\nmultiplies their holonomies (`holonomy_append`); the composite is flat.\nA surface tiled by flat plaquettes therefore has flat boundary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.isFlatPlaquette_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.isFlatPlaquette_one","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L114-L115","doc":"The trivial (constant) loop is flat. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.isFlatPlaquette_pureGauge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.isFlatPlaquette_pureGauge","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L110-L112","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.IsFlatPlaquette","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.IsFlatPlaquette","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L104-L108","doc":"**Discrete curvature defect** of a square plaquette: the boundary\nholonomy itself, measured against the identity.  The connection is *flat*\nat the plaquette iff this equals `1`; `loopHolonomyPureGauge_eq_one` says\nevery exact connection is flat. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.loopHolonomyPureGauge_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.loopHolonomyPureGauge_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L94-L102","doc":"**Flatness of a pure-gauge connection** — the discrete non-abelian\n`d² = 0` / Stokes flatness: an exact (pure-gauge) connection has trivial\nplaquette holonomy, so its discrete curvature vanishes.  Proved by group\ntelescoping. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.loopHolonomyPureGauge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.loopHolonomyPureGauge","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L82-L92","doc":"**Plaquette holonomy of a pure-gauge (exact) connection.**\n\nAssign group elements `h₀, h₁, h₂, h₃` to the four vertices of a square\nand take the connection to be *exact / pure gauge*: the transport along\nthe edge from vertex `i` to vertex `j` is `hᵢ * hⱼ⁻¹` (a discrete\ngradient).  The boundary holonomy of the square loop\n`v₀ → v₁ → v₂ → v₃ → v₀` is the ordered product of the four edge\ntransports, listed in path order (the first edge `v₀ → v₁` leftmost, per\nthe `holonomy` convention). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.holonomy_reverse_map_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.holonomy_reverse_map_inv","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L74-L80","doc":"**Reverse path gives the inverse holonomy.**  Traversing the path\nbackwards with each segment transport inverted yields the inverse of the\nforward holonomy — the discrete statement that the holonomy of `γ⁻¹` is\n`(hol γ)⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.holonomy_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.holonomy_append","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L66-L72","doc":"**Concatenation multiplicativity** — the composition law of the\nnon-abelian line integral: the holonomy of a path split into an initial\npiece `p` followed by `q` is the ordered product of the two holonomies.\nThis is the discrete non-abelian Stokes composition along paths. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.holonomy_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.holonomy_cons","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L62-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.holonomy_singleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.holonomy_singleton","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L59-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.holonomy_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.holonomy_nil","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.holonomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration.holonomy","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/YekutieliIntegration.lean#L47-L55","doc":"**Path-ordered product (discrete non-abelian line integral).**\n\nThe holonomy of a path presented as an ordered list of segment\ntransports `[g₀, g₁, …, g_{n-1}]` is their ordered product\n`g₀ * g₁ * … * g_{n-1}` — segments composed in path order.  This is the\ndiscrete / lattice realisation of the path-ordered exponential\n`P exp ∫_γ A`; the continuum limit (mesh → 0) is analytic and is *not*\nformalised here. ","signatureChunk":0}]}